1) Run 2min rollouts on the pose-duplex student and the audio-duplex conversational partner. Use the same rollout settings as before, no changes, same number of nodes, optimal audio-dup sampling, etc. 
2) Score the pose generations of the pose-duplex model with pose-monoplex. Pose mono should have CFG with guidance of 3 (meaning that the pose mono needs to do two forwards per scoring, same as last time). 
3) Score the audio and pose with a frozen checkpoint of the student that we start from. this self-teacher will see all of the context that the student sees. No cfg. Here we will do a forward KL, ie, sample on the frozen teacher. 
4) Keep a KL of 3e-6 for the backbone, 1e-5 for the pose tower and 1e-5 for the pose light. 
5) Do the same setup where we do 8 light micros accumulated into one upper step. 
6) Weigh the codebooks at 1:1 cb0 to cb1-31, same as pretrain. 
7) Do audio training only on 1/8 of the lights (same as the pretraining, copy whatever is used there). 
8) Keep the same prefil and conditioning setup as the last training run. 
9) Put the run on the same dashboard. 
10) Keep the same ratio of category and lexical loss that is used in the pretrain. 
11) save checkpoints every 2 hours, and set a necessary save for 11:50pm san francisco time today. Keep the latest optimizer state on hf. 

