INSERT INTO "threads" VALUES('01a184bd-f7d9-7061-850c-797fbf83136f','/home/param/.codex/sessions/2026/10/28/rollout-2026-10-28T23-00-04-01a184bd-f7d9-7061-850c-797fbf83136f.jsonl',1793228404,1793253836,'vscode','openai','/home/param/pose-repo','I want to know how kosher certain posttraining methods that I am interested in trying are. Here is the basic setup: I have trained this text-to-pose model which takes a full text transcript upfront and then generated speech and pose tokens frame by frame. I want to use this guy as a teacher to improve a causal, temporal model which generaetes its own text, audio, and pose frame by frame. the first idea that I had was to just run rollouts on the student, provide the full transcript to the teacher upfront and then do opd on the pose tokens. but this presents an advantage to the teacher: it has access to some information that the student does not have. So, we would have to do some hacks like, eg, doing forward kl instead of reverse (ie, do the KL with p(teacher) not p(steudent) since the teacher should ideally have a more narrow distribution and hence the other way around would have massive losses from the teacher just not having support over some region since it is more strongly conditioned) .
